WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:06.720
Let's take a closer look at shoulder
seams when working cut and sew.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.500
In this sample, I've knit
a back and two cardigan fronts.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.500
I scrapped off the shoulders.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:21.980
Each has 20 stitches, and I scrapped
off the neck openings separately.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.800
Now, for this sample,
I then used a template to mark the neck

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:31.300
openings, but this is a case
of "do as I say, not as I did."

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:35.720
What I should have done was join the
shoulders, then marked the neck opening.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:46.900
Either way, you can see my shoulder
join with the waste yarn removed.

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:49.160
The marks and the upcoming stitch lines

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:54.140
are carefully positioned away
from that shoulder seam.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:58.920
I left my orange neck
opening waste yarn in place.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:05.080
You could also choose to bind off the neck
openings, but this whole area is going

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:10.120
to be cut away and the raw edges
will be enclosed with my band.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.680
Here is the single line
of straight stitches.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:20.320
Notice that I did not sew
those shoulder seam stitches.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:26.340
Then a line or two of zig -zag should
be enough to secure my stitches.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:32.360
Notice that I didn't stitch
along those shoulder stitches.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.720
When using a serger,

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:40.640
you have to be extra careful not
to stitch those shoulder stitches.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:44.120
The secret here is to isolate those

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:48.420
shoulder stitches when stitching
and cutting the neckline.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.740
Now, it's difficult to see in this photo,

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:55.380
but when hanging the neck edge
on the machine to form the band,

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:59.780
care needs to be taken to secure
those shoulder stitches.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:03.850
Even though we stretch the neckline when
hanging it on the machine for

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:09.660
a neat finish, don't stretch
in that shoulder seam area.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.500
Once you finish the band,

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:15.760
the neck edge should be neat and tidy
along those secure shoulder seams.

